---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const sections = [
  ['overview','Overview'],['services','Services & eligibility'],['orders','Orders & approval'],['payment','Pricing & payment'],['publishers','Publisher control'],['content','Content responsibilities'],['delivery','Delivery & revisions'],['guarantees','Guarantees'],['seo','SEO outcomes'],['liability','Liability'],['changes','Changes & contact']
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service | Web Grouth" description="Detailed terms for Web Grouth guest posting, link insertion, pay-after-live orders and publisher placements.">
  <div class="saas-page">
    <section class="saas-hero"><div class="shell saas-hero-grid"><div class="saas-hero-copy" data-reveal><div class="saas-breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Terms</span></div><span class="saas-kicker">Legal & service terms</span><h1>Clear rules for a <span>clearer campaign.</span></h1><p>These Terms of Service explain how Web Grouth enquiries, approvals, publisher placements, payments and campaign protections are handled.</p></div><aside class="saas-hero-panel" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1"><span>Document information</span><ul><li>Effective date <span>31 August 2026</span></li><li>Business <span>Web Grouth</span></li><li>Primary service <span>Guest posting</span></li><li>Contact <span>nasirhaiderseo@gmail.com</span></li></ul></aside></div></section>
    <section class="saas-section"><div class="shell legal-layout">
      <aside class="legal-toc"><strong>On this page</strong><nav>{sections.map(([id,label]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>)}</nav></aside>
      <article class="legal-content">
        <p class="legal-note">Order-specific written terms, including website, price, turnaround, link attributes and guarantee eligibility, form part of these Terms. If a confirmed order term conflicts with a general statement here, the confirmed order term controls for that placement.</p>
        <section id="overview"><h2>1. Overview and acceptance</h2><p>These Terms apply when you access Webgrouth.com, submit an enquiry or order, approve a publisher placement, or purchase a service from Web Grouth. By proceeding with an approved order, you confirm that you have authority to act for the relevant website or client and agree to these Terms.</p><p>If you do not agree, do not submit content for publication or approve a placement. Website browsing alone does not create a paid service relationship.</p></section>
        <section id="services"><h2>2. Services and eligibility</h2><p>Web Grouth provides guest post placement, contextual link insertion, publisher outreach, content support, bulk fulfilment and related off-page SEO services. Availability depends on niche, content, target URL, publisher rules, geography, budget and campaign risk.</p><ul><li>Websites shown in previews are illustrative until a specific publisher is confirmed.</li><li>Metrics such as DA, DR and traffic may come from third-party tools and can change.</li><li>The $0 advance model applies only where confirmed for the relevant order.</li><li>Restricted, misleading, unlawful or publisher-prohibited campaigns may be declined.</li></ul></section>
        <section id="orders"><h2>3. Orders, approval and scope</h2><p>An order begins when the parties confirm the required website or selection criteria, target URL, anchor text, content responsibility, price and essential placement terms. A submitted website form is a request for review, not automatic acceptance.</p><p>You are responsible for checking the selected site and instructions before approval. Changes requested after a publisher has accepted or published content may require additional time, cost or a new order.</p></section>
        <section id="payment"><h2>4. Pricing and payment</h2><p>Prices may be stated per placement, per campaign or through a custom quotation. Unless stated otherwise, prices cover only the confirmed deliverables. Bank, payment processor, currency conversion or tax charges may apply separately.</p><h3>Pay-after-live orders</h3><p>For an eligible $0 advance order, payment becomes due after Web Grouth provides the agreed live URL and confirms that the placement matches the approved core instructions. Payment should be completed within the timeframe stated in the order confirmation.</p><h3>Other orders</h3><p>Some publishers, restricted niches, content-heavy projects or custom outreach campaigns may require partial or full advance payment. Any such requirement must be disclosed before approval.</p></section>
        <section id="publishers"><h2>5. Publisher and third-party control</h2><p>Publishers retain editorial and technical control of their websites. They may reject content, edit headlines or copy, change publication schedules, update policies, migrate pages or remove content. Web Grouth will communicate material conditions that are known before the order is approved.</p><p>Web Grouth does not own or control third-party SEO metric providers, search engines, hosting services, payment processors, email delivery tools or WhatsApp.</p></section>
        <section id="content"><h2>6. Client and content responsibilities</h2><p>You must provide accurate URLs, lawful claims, usable anchor instructions and content that does not infringe intellectual property, privacy, advertising or other rights. You must disclose regulated or restricted topics before approval.</p><ul><li>Do not submit malware, deceptive redirects, illegal products or impersonation content.</li><li>Do not require claims that cannot be reasonably supported.</li><li>Provide timely feedback when approval or clarification is requested.</li><li>Maintain a working target page for the intended placement.</li></ul></section>
        <section id="delivery"><h2>7. Delivery, turnaround and revisions</h2><p>Turnaround time is an estimate unless expressly confirmed as a fixed deadline. Publisher response, editorial review, holidays, content revisions and technical issues may affect timing.</p><p>A delivery is considered complete when the agreed content and link are available at the supplied live URL, subject to the confirmed placement terms. Reasonable corrections relating to an incorrect agreed URL, anchor or link attribute should be reported promptly.</p></section>
        <section id="guarantees"><h2>8. Indexation and replacement protection</h2><p>Eligible placements may include a 30-day indexation policy and a six-month link replacement window. These protections are governed by the separate <a href="/guarantee-policy">Indexation & Replacement Guarantee Policy</a>, including eligibility, exclusions and claim steps.</p><p>No protection applies unless it is included in the written order terms. A replacement is normally the first remedy for an eligible removed link.</p></section>
        <section id="seo"><h2>9. SEO outcomes and third-party metrics</h2><p>Web Grouth does not guarantee rankings, organic traffic, leads, revenue, domain metrics or search-engine treatment. SEO outcomes are affected by algorithms, competitors, content, technical quality, market conditions and many factors outside a single placement.</p><p>DA, DR, traffic estimates, index status and similar values represent a point-in-time check and may differ between tools or change after approval.</p></section>
        <section id="liability"><h2>10. Liability and service limits</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Web Grouth is not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, including lost rankings, traffic, profit, opportunity or reputation resulting from publisher or search-engine actions.</p><p>For a paid affected order, Web Grouth's aggregate direct liability is limited to the amount paid for that specific affected service, except where a limitation is prohibited by law.</p></section>
        <section id="changes"><h2>11. Changes, governing arrangements and contact</h2><p>These Terms may be updated as the service, publisher requirements or applicable practices change. The effective date at the top identifies the current website version. Material order changes will not retroactively remove a protection already confirmed in writing.</p><p>Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:nasirhaiderseo@gmail.com">nasirhaiderseo@gmail.com</a>, through <a href="/contact">the contact page</a>, or by WhatsApp at <a href="https://wa.me/923327810261">+92 332 7810261</a>.</p></section>
      </article>
    </div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
